A build also carries parts of the system it was made on: the Python
interpreter with the libraries it uses, and on Linux the system
libraries that the X11 window system plugin needs. The licence text of
each is written into the build, in resources/licenses/system/, and the
About window shows them with the others.

An AppImage starts with the AppImage runtime (MIT License), which
contains musl libc, libfuse, squashfuse, zstd and zlib. Its licence
notice is in the AppImage with the others.
    https://github.com/AppImage/type2-runtime

